{
  "name": "cricket",
  "_about": "A cricket -- the field cricket (Gryllus campestris), 2.3 cm long: stout and glossy black; a big round head with very long thread antennae, longer than the body; a broad box of a pronotum; the forewings lying flat on the back and folded down at the sides, their bases yellow, the male's veined into a singing file; two long cerci at the tail (and the female's long needle ovipositor -- the variant); thick hind femora, red beneath. Coat: the house cricket (Acheta domesticus, straw-brown). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
